{"en":[{"partOfSpeech":"Noun","language":"English","definitions":[{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt15\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> Any of certain types of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/outerwear\" title=\"outerwear\">outerwear</a>.\n<ol><li>A piece of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/clothing\" title=\"clothing\">clothing</a> worn on the upper body outside a shirt or blouse, often waist length to thigh length.</li>\n<li>A piece of a person's <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/suit\" title=\"suit\">suit</a>, beside <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/trousers\" title=\"trousers\">trousers</a> and, sometimes, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/waistcoat\" title=\"waistcoat\">waistcoat</a>; coat .</li>\n<li>An outer garment (usually white) intended for <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/chef\" title=\"chef\">chefs</a> and which may be taken to signify status.</li>\n<li><span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt17\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> A <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/vest\" title=\"vest\">vest</a> ; a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/waistcoat\" title=\"waistcoat\">waistcoat</a> .</li>\n<li><span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt20\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> A <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/letter_jacket\" title=\"letter jacket\">letter jacket</a>.","parsedExamples":[{"example":"He's hoping to earn his <b>jacket</b> this year."}],"examples":["He's hoping to earn his <b>jacket</b> this year."]},{"definition":"A piece of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/clothing\" title=\"clothing\">clothing</a> worn on the upper body outside a shirt or blouse, often waist length to thigh length."},{"definition":"A piece of a person's <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/suit\" title=\"suit\">suit</a>, beside <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/trousers\" title=\"trousers\">trousers</a> and, sometimes, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/waistcoat\" title=\"waistcoat\">waistcoat</a>; coat .